notion-jumptosearch:
Accessibility skip link that jumps to the site search field in the page header. It stays visually hidden until it receives keyboard focus.

See also
* {{msg-mw|Search}}

notion-main-menu-label:
Heading of the main menu panel, which holds the wiki's site navigation links.

The key name is derived at runtime from the pinnable element ID <code>notion-main-menu</code>, so it cannot be renamed independently of that ID.

{{Identical|Main menu}}

notion-toc-label:
Heading of the table of contents panel, shown above the list of the sections of the page.

The key name is derived at runtime from the pinnable element ID <code>notion-toc</code>, so it cannot be renamed independently of that ID.

{{Identical|Contents}}

notion-page-tools-label:
Label of the page tools pinnable panel, which groups the tools and actions that apply to the page currently being viewed.

The key name is derived at runtime from the pinnable element ID <code>notion-page-tools</code>, so it cannot be renamed independently of that ID.

{{Identical|Tools}}

tooltip-notion-anon-user-menu-title:
Used as the title attribute for the user menu icon in the page header, shown on hover to anonymous (logged-out) readers.

The <code>tooltip-</code> prefix is structural rather than descriptive: the skin calls <code>Linker::tooltip( 'notion-anon-user-menu-title' )</code>, which prepends <code>tooltip-</code> to the key it is given, so this key cannot be renamed or grouped with the other <code>notion-</code> keys.

{{Identical|More options}}

notion-pin-element-aria-label:
Accessible label (<code>aria-label</code>) for the button that moves (pins) a panel into the sidebar. Never shown on screen; unlike the visible label {{msg-mw|notion-pin-element-label}} it names the panel that the button acts on.

Parameters:
* $1 – the label of the element being moved, for example {{msg-mw|notion-toc-label}} or {{msg-mw|notion-appearance-label}}

notion-unpin-element-aria-label:
Accessible label (<code>aria-label</code>) for the button that hides (unpins) a panel from the sidebar. Never shown on screen; unlike the visible label {{msg-mw|notion-unpin-element-label}} it names the panel that the button acts on.

Parameters:
* $1 – the label of the element being hidden, for example {{msg-mw|notion-toc-label}} or {{msg-mw|notion-appearance-label}}

notion-feature-limited-width-name:
Heading label for the content width setting in the appearance menu. The title of a list that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-0-label}}

notion-feature-limited-width-0-label:
Label for the option that turns limited width off, so that the content fills the whole width of the browser window. An item in a list that has the title {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-name}} and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-0-label}}

notion-feature-limited-width-1-label:
Label for the option that turns limited width on, so that the reading column keeps a comfortable line length on wide screens. An item in a list that has the title {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-name}} and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-limited-width-0-label}}

{{Identical|Standard}}

notion-feature-custom-font-size-name:
Heading label for the text size setting in the appearance menu. The title of a list that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-0-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-2-label}}

notion-feature-custom-font-size-0-label:
Label for the smallest of the three text sizes. An item in a list that has the title {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-name}} and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-0-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-2-label}}

notion-feature-custom-font-size-1-label:
Label for the middle of the three text sizes. Despite the English wording it is not the default: readers who have chosen nothing get the smallest size. An item in a list that has the title {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-name}} and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-0-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-2-label}}

{{Identical|Standard}}

notion-feature-custom-font-size-2-label:
Label for the largest of the three text sizes. An item in a list that has the title {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-name}} and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-0-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-1-label}}
* {{msg-mw|notion-feature-custom-font-size-2-label}}

skin-theme-name:
Heading label for the colour setting in the appearance menu, which switches between the light and dark colour themes. The title of a list that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-os-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-day-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-night-label}}

This key is deliberately not prefixed with <code>notion-</code>: it is shared with the Vector skin, and both skins define it with the same English text so that the rendered wording cannot change with the order in which the two skins are loaded. Never change the English value on one side only.

skin-theme-day-label:
Label for the light colour theme, which is the standard one. A part of the list that has the title {{msg-mw|skin-theme-name}}, and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-os-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-day-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-night-label}}

This key is deliberately not prefixed with <code>notion-</code>: it is shared with the Vector skin, and both skins define it with the same English text so that the rendered wording cannot change with the order in which the two skins are loaded. Never change the English value on one side only.

skin-theme-night-label:
Label for the dark (night) colour theme, which reduces the light emitted by the screen. A part of the list that has the title {{msg-mw|skin-theme-name}}, and that includes the following items:
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-os-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-day-label}}
* {{msg-mw|skin-theme-night-label}}

This key is deliberately not prefixed with <code>notion-</code>: it is shared with the Vector skin, and both skins define it with the same English text so that the rendered wording cannot change with the order in which the two skins are loaded. Never change the English value on one side only.

notion-prefs-limited-width-help:
Help message used on [[Special:Preferences]], shown beneath the checkbox labelled {{msg-mw|notion-prefs-limited-width}}.

